      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-08-08_WidnesExaminer_art0126" n="art0126">
        <p>ANOTHER RAILWAY ACCIDENT AT</p>
        <p>PRESTON.</p>
        <p>Preston was en Monday the scene of a second fatal railway accident. It appears that about nine o'clock in the morning a Lancashire and Yorkshire Company's ex- cursion from Leeds to Blackpool was standing in a loop at the junction where the line branchesoff to Blackburn. A West Lancashire Company's train was coming from Southport, when, it is alleged, through the mistaking of a signal, the driver of the excursion train started his en- gine. A collision occurred at the points, the Lancashire and Yorkshire engine completely smashing a saloon in the middle of the West Lancashire train and killing one of the occupants, William Eatcr, aged 34, who lived near Chorley. Another occupant WWI severely hurt,and five other' people in the train received injuries. No one in the excursion train appears to have suffered.</p>
      </div>
