ithubarb : 1, B Parker. Helsby ; 2, R Dilworth, Alvailley. C, lery : 1, T Rawles, Alvanley • 2, R Dilwsrth. Brosci Bean : 1. R Dilworth ; 2, T Rowles. Scarlet runners, 1, Mrs Whalley, Helsby ; 2, Mrs Whiteley. Belsby. Dwarf beans: 1, Mrs Whalley; 2, R. Dilworth. Peas :1, T Wright Alvanley ; 2, R Dilworth. Carrots : 1, R Dilworth. Spring onions 1, It Dilworth ; 2, T Rowles. Autumn onions : 1., it Dilworth Ki ney potatoes: 1, P. Wright, Helsby; 2, TWr ght ;3, n Dilworth. It mud pota- toes: 1 T Wright; 2, F Wright. Collection of vegetables : 2. T Brandreth, tielaby. Marrows : 1, Mrs Whttel .v ; 2, Mrs Whalley. Apples: 1, B Parker 2, Mrs White- ley; h c. Mrs Whiteley. Pears : 1, Eleanor Wrieht, Al- vanley ; 2. B Parker. Raspberries : 1, T Brandreth ; 2, 'V Rowles. Red currants :1. T Rovrles. Roses: 1 A J Briant. Helsby '• 2, Mrs Whitelsy Pussies; 1, Mrs Jas. Taylor, Helsby ;2, A J Briant, Violas 1, A J Bri tnt ;2' Mrs Jas. Taylor. Three window plants ; 1. Mr, Whiteley. One window plant; 1, B Parker. Fern: 1, W G Risketts 2. E 3 Briant. Sweet peas 1, T Brandreth 2, Eleanor Wright. Cut flowers : 1. Mrs James Taylor ;2. A J Briant. Children's classes.-For those under twelve years. Wild flowers and grasses: 1, John Dunbabin, Hel-by ;2, A Dun- babin. Helsby .;3, Leonard Wright. Helsby: v.h.c. Alice Walker, Alvsn.ey. Fanny Jones, Helsby, Elizabeth Brit- land, Helsby ; hc . Lillie Ricketts, Ince, Edward Britland, Alvanley ; Jot eph Nixon, Ifelsby ; Frank Nixon, Helsby. Over twelve years: 1, Evelyn Greenway, Alvanley: 2, Ig Dunbthin, Helsby ;3, W Beech, Helsby ; 4, William Lockett, Helsby. Open Cass.-Collection of vegetables : 1, James Whi'e, Heisbv_.• 2, T Grime, Helsby. Mangolds : 1. I` Wright; 2, It Jeffs, Ifsesford. Swede turnips : 1, W Ligh f tot ; 2, S H 'Models, Alvanley. Beans : 1, Mrs James Reynolds, Frod- sham. Onions: 1, T Grime ; 2, Mrs James Reynolds. Round potatoes ; 1, 3 1-1 Node, .2, G F Taylor. rielsby. Kidney potatoes 1. H Wright, Alvanlev ;2, S H Noden. Marrows : 1, Mss F Guest, Heisby ;2, James White :3. '3 F Tavlsr. Shallots : 1, T Grime ;9, Miss B Guest. Peas :1, G F Taylor ;2, James White. Tomatoei : 1. James White ; 2, Mrs James Reynolds. Gooseberries : 1. Mrs G C Taylor, Helsby ;2, James White. Collection of fruit 1, K E Gar- nett, Helsby ;2. James White. Roses : 1. Mrs G C Taylor ; 2, Ii E Garnett. Carnations : 1, T Fletcher, Htesby ; 2, James White. Bouquet: Mrs James Taylor. Sprays and buttonholes: Mr James Taylor. Z male pelargoniums : 1, Mrs G C Taylor ; 2, E J Besant. Group of greenhouse plants : 1, James White ;2, A J Besant. Six ferns :1, Mrs C Taylor. Gresnhouse plant in flower : 1, B J Secant ; 2, James Whit Folia se plant; 1, Mrs James Tavler ;2, IL (3 Garnett ; 3, Miss Grime, He'sby. Specimen fern : 1, A J Besant ;2, Mrs G C Taylor. Collection of apples: 1. Miss B Guest ;2. R Jeffs ; 3, C ffyder. Elton pears : I, James White ; 2. IS Blythe. Helsby. Best kept cottage garden: 1, C Clay :2, G Thompson, Helsby. Ladies' table &amp;creation : 1, Miss 14 Guest ; 2. Mrs Wliall9e ; h c, Mrs Spafford, Helsby. Couple of fowls : 1. Mrs R Dilworth 2 Mrs Ellams, Helsby. Eggs • 1. George J mes. Frodsharn ; 2, John Hoplev hc. Margaret Edwards. Alvaniev. Batter, 1, Mrs Alexander, Alvanley ; 2, Mrs W Davies. Helsby. Jam, ctetagers' : 1, Mrs It Beech. Helsby ; 2, 'Mrs Harnaman. JAM (open) : 1, Mrs James Taylor; 2, Miss 3.1 J Wright, Alvanley. Outdoor tomatoes :1. James White; 2, Airs Griffiass, Helsb).</p>
