        <p>WEEKLY CHAT. SUBJECT THE BOGGART HOLE CLOUGH PROSECUTIONS. At the present Moment every citizen is interested in the doings of the I L.P.. and what will be the outcome .of the present proceedings at the City Police Court. WILL CERTAIN GENTLEMEN AND LADIES be allowed to do as they like, or will they have to rest? This is the question of the moment Mr. W. H. WORSI.ItY himself believes in free speech, but not in obstruction, and had the following questions been asked at the Boggart Hole Clough any of the last few Sundays :—Who is the most successful man in the , city ? Who is the ke nest buyer living? Who is the real benefactor to the workingman? the answer would have been —WON. LEY, the KONEER of the £1 and 220 Houses of urnitiire I Now, he has a crowd of imitators. All his com- petitors follow his lead like a flock of sheep; not cue has any origin .lity. They watch his dvertiserrients, and pouni eon any new idea, filching the proluct of his brain, in conse- quence of an entire absence of that necessary qualification to success.</p>
