        <p>CAUTION. kJ Beware of buying new London jerry-built Furniture, No mAler how low thi. price is, it is near at any price. WOBSLEY'S have becond-hand reliable Furniture, by good makers, which will last for ages. There is no disputing the fact that High-class 6second-hand Furniture is better than new The only fault is that sometimes the aria eis old- fashioned. This is easily remedied at WOHSLEY'b. They have over 600 ct,binet-makers at work modernising Se 'ond- band Furniture where neoessary. For instance, Second-hand Bide: oarda are easily modernised by aving the backs raised, the plates bevelled, and the pan.ls carved. You need never fear cracking, blistering, grub-eaten, or moth-eaten Furniture at Worsley's. tecond-hand Furniture is not troubled with ese complaints. They give a written warranty for 10 years with all turnishmig orders.</p>
        <p>NEW FURNITURE. All WORSLEI'S New Furniture is their °an make. Of court e it is obviously lin, ossib[es to supply every require- ment .tecond-hanel. Worsley's have, therefore, erected a Cabinet works in City-road, with an immense stock of seasoned timber for the production of reliable Furniture. Every item in the Bedding Department is new, guaranteed pure, under minute inspection. TEEMS. The terms are principally cash, and all the prices adver- tised are fixe at the lowest figure. So thoroughly are we convinced that the Hire System is baneful and ruinous to the purchaser that in March of 1894 we inaugurated our New Credit System of DEFERRED PAYMENTS to combat and crush the Hire System. County Court J ,dges have freely expressed opinions re the Hire System, which have been any- thing but complimentary to tho,e trading under this system. The enormous amounts charged, and the arbitrary restric- tions contained in the agreements are an outrage on the cre- dulity of the purchaser. Worsley's, therefore, detetmined to blot it out in Manchester by allowing respectable purchasers to buy in the cheapest market,'• VIM PANTHEON," at their advertited cash prices, and allow relsonable time to pay by deferred payments, charging only 10 per cent extra for the convenience. Any of our rovertised bargains can be bought on these terms. It is a sufficient proof gf the popularity of our System when we say that we urnished over 400 heuses on this New redit System during n:ne months of 1894. 940 houses clurit,g the year 01 1895, and already over 600 houses during this year, all ot which have been satisfactory to both' ourselves and the put, hqsers. Wher, purchasin ' you need not say you require credit; buy as if for cash, and only men- tion how you wish to pay when the purchases are completed, for there is only one price at "The PANTHEON."</p>
        <p>PENNY SAVED IS A PENNY MADE." How to save money—Waste not, want not. Don't nisi' ou the Hire Sysfem, with its extravagant high prices •,rbitrary mg eements and lespotic restrictions. For instance, suppose A furnishes for £ICO on the hire system with 8, and pays B £99 in instalments, but neglects to pay B the last instalment in time, the agreem-nt gives B the power to forcibly re-take pow stion of toe furniture, but the whole of the £99 paid is then ferteited to B ; cohsequently B gets both money and goods. In ad 'ition to the above disadvantages, the price charged is exorbitant, often 200 and 300 per cent. more than tor cash at a pro er establishment It is high time this system was declired illegal. Be it known that at WORSLEY'S. THE PANTHEON. OAYTHORN. MANC ES- TER, high-class New and seeond-hand Furniture may be had at the exact advertisfxl marked cash price, no less under any circumstanc«s. Also, that in cases where it is inconvenient to pay the whole of the money d .wn, WORSLEY'S are pre- pared to assist purchasers by allowing the account to be paid at convenient intervals, cha•ging only a small percentage for the privilege. By this means the purchaser knows exactly what he is charged for the goods and esf apes fear and trembling as to the loss of lais furniture, if he happens to miss a paymest W oIISLEY'S have on view complete House of Furniture for 15 guineas. £2O £3O, £4O, £lOO, £250, £350 and £5O), full particultrs of which are supplied cost free. " THE PANTHEON "is packed from floor to ceiling with countless bargain in Dining, Drawing, Skting, Bedroom, Office, and Library Furniture by Lamb, Gillows, Ogden, Garnett, &amp;c. Read the following bargains:—</p>
