        <p>WEEKLY REPORT ON THE 21EILTII OF WARRINGTON. During last week, which was the 30th, of the current year, the following births and deaths were registered : Births. Deaths. Warrington 3O 37 Latchford Total 35 40 The excess of deaths over births was 5. The death rate from all causes was equal to 358 per I,ooo,against 12 05 the average of the previous four weeks,and against 5 4 the corresponding week of last year. The death rate from the seven chief zynaotic diseases was equal to 8-9 per .1,000, against 06 the average rate of the four previous weeks, and against 0-9 the corresponding week of 1895. The ages of mortality were- 0— 1 1-5 5-15 15-25 25-65 65 up. 14 3 2 18 3 40 The deaths included-10 from diarrhoea., 1 influenza, 6 from phihisis, 1 from old age, 7 from brain disease, 1 from heart disease, 2 from lung disease. The following cases of infectious disease have bee n reported during the week :—Smalipox 1 case, scarlet fever 1 case, erysipelas 1 case, enteric fever 1 case, puerperal 1 case. Total number of patients in hospital on Saturday, July 25th, 15. METEOROLOGY.—The mean temperature was 62' Fah., and therefore 1 degree higher than the preceding, week. The maximem temperature 80 FA., was re- corded on the 21st inst., and the minimum tempera- ture 47F., on the 21st inst. The Rainfall measured one inch. The general direc- tion was S.W., the reading of the Anemometer denoting 1440 miles. JOHN H. GOHNALL, Medical Officer of Health. P.S.—The sudden increase in the death rate is due to Autumnal Diarrhcea. NORTHERN RUGBY UNION. A meeting of the Committee of the Northern Rugby Football Union was held on Tuesday night at the Spread Eagle Hotel, Manchester, Mr. H. H. Waller (Brighouse) in the chair. Applications tor membership were re- ceived from Thornton Rangers, Bradford Churchill; Bradford and District Competition, Salford St. Bartho- lomew's, Allerton. Stockpsrt Rangers, Oldham League, and Broughton Recreation. The whole of the clubs were admitted by the unanimous vote of the Committee. l'he pay of the subscriptions was fixed "on or before August 31," and the draw for the cup for September 3. The general meeting will be held at Huddersfield on the 27th of the present month.</p>
